{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVjVzcRBpkmZLnPpnNeV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about error handling in a batch processing loop. They want to understand what happens when an authentication token expires mid-batch:\n\nLooking at the code:\n```python\nfor page in pages:\n    for item in page.items:\n        client.push(item, token=token)   # raises AuthExpired\n    checkpoint(page.id)\n```\n\nThe checkpoint is called at the page level (after all items in the page are pushed). So if the token expires mid-batch (in the middle of processing items), an `AuthExpired` exception will be raised and will propagate up. The checkpoint for that page will never be called because the exception happens before the checkpoint.\n\nSo the behavior is:\n- If the token expires while processing item N in page P, the exception will propagate\n- The checkpoint won't be called for page P\n- On retry/resume, it will restart from page P (and re-process all items in that page, including items that were successfully pushed before the token expired)\n\nThis is a common issue with batch processing - partial batches. The code lacks atomicity at the batch level. Items already pushed will be pushed again.\n\nThe user is asking where the loop \"leaves off\" - they want to know the resume point.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6945,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6945},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"4f04c926-a1b9-4707-949f-7126a43d7a62","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:40:31.204Z","request_id":"req_011CdVjVyhrHpF59QT6aqDEU"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVjVzcRBpkmZLnPpnNeV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"If the token expires mid-batch, it **restarts the entire page**, not the failed item.\n\nThe `checkpoint(page.id)` only fires after all items in a page succeed. Since the exception propagates before that point, no checkpoint is saved for page P. On resume, you'd replay page P from the start, re-pushing items that already went through before the token expired.\n\n**The issues:**\n\n1. **Duplicate pushes** — items before the failure get pushed twice (once before expiry, once on retry)\n2. **No fine-grained recovery** — can't resume mid-page; must restart the whole page\n\n**To fix it, checkpoint per item:**\n\n```python\nfor page in pages:\n    for item in page.items:\n        client.push(item, token=token)   # raises AuthExpired\n        checkpoint(item.id)  # checkpoint after each item succeeds\n```\n\nOr group checkpoints and skip already-processed items on retry:\n\n```python\nprocessed = set(load_processed_ids())  # restore from prior run\nfor page in pages:\n    for item in page.items:\n        if item.id in processed:\n            continue\n        client.push(item, token=token)\n        processed.add(item.id)\n        checkpoint(item.id)\n```\n\nThe first approach is simpler if your checkpoint storage is cheap (usually is)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6945,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6945},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"88c9825f-dffc-4608-bf7c-374f73309271","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:40:34.283Z","request_id":"req_011CdVjVyhrHpF59QT6aqDEU"}
